  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on an aspiration level calculated as the mean of all outcomes, ignoring probabilities. The outcomes in the decision problem are 4000, 0 (from Lottery A), and 3000 (from Lottery B). The mean of these outcomes is (4000 + 0 + 3000) / 3 = 2333.33 Euros. This is the aspiration level. Next, the differences between each outcome and the aspiration level are computed: 4000 - 2333.33 = +1666.67; 0 - 2333.33 = -2333.33; 3000 - 2333.33 = +666.67. A 'positive difference' occurs when an outcome exceeds the aspiration level. Lottery A has a positive difference only in the 4000 outcome (80% probability), so its probability of a positive difference is 80%. Lottery B has a positive difference in the 3000 outcome (100% probability), so its probability of a positive difference is 100%. The reason prefers the lottery with the higher probability of positive differences, which is Lottery B. Thus, the reason can be applied and would lead to choosing B.",
